Z||000000||FieroSoul||07-14-2001||10:58 AM||||  I finally got curious enough to decode my VIN code. Now I am more confused than usual.  My 4 & 5 digits are AM which according to Haynes I have a 6000 Fiero sport coupe.  I think I have regular coupe. Is Haynes out to lunch???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-14-2001||11:46 AM||||Are you sure that the fourth digit is an 'A'? All Fieros have a 'P' as the fourth digit (hence the P-body designation).||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||07-14-2001||12:15 PM||||Once you are sure you have the correct VIN, go here to check it out:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/vin.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/vin.html</A> <P>FieroSoul -- I spent a lot of time over in Panama City last week as my son was playing in a baseball tourney at GCC.  Didn't see any Fieros over that way though.  In fact, in all my trips over there, the only one I have seen is a white notchback in Ft Walton Beach.  Have seen him a couple of times as I passed thru on 98....<P><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSoul||07-14-2001||06:36 PM||||  Yes, I am sure it is an A. The VIN decoder that mbramble provided also decoded it a Fiero P body sport coupe.  Maybe some were given that A code. Interesting.  Thanks for the help guys.  By the way there are a few Fieros here (obviously I'm one) but we aren't organized. I know of about 10.  Maybe someday we will get together. <BR>[This message has been edited by FieroSoul (edited 07-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroSoul (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||theogre||07-14-2001||11:17 PM||||An A???? Are you sure that thing has it's original VIN tag on the dash??? You should dig around the car and check it aginst the other plates. I'm not aware of any Fiero the should have an A in position 4. If the other VIN plates are gone you need to be finding out what is up.<P>The first 4 characters of all Fiero should all be 1G2P. ones made for Canada may be 2G2P.<P>In the VIN sheet I have AM in slots 4 and 5 would make it an Old Cutlas Ciera Brougham<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSoul||07-15-2001||08:15 AM||||  Ok, Ogre. I looked at the door plate.  The last 4 of the serial # are no longer readable but the rest matches. I found another plate under the bonnet and it matches perfectly. I am certain I have seen a number stamped somewhere but can remember the location. Anyplace else I can check w/o dismantling the car? <P>  1G2AM37R6EP32XXXX<BR> <BR>  BTW, my eyes are pretty good and I am certain it is an A.  The decoder that mbramble supplied decoded it fine as a Fiero sport coupe, didn't even hiccup.  Maybe I have something unusual, maybe not. <P>Anyone else have an A in position 4???  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ginoferrari||07-15-2001||03:37 PM||||I have an A at position 4 then an M. I was wondering what the difference between a coupe and a sport coupe was. I've had my 84 2M4 since 86 and just found this site and think it's a wealth of information. I only registered today and am looking forward to spending a lot of time here getting info on my favorite Fiero. I plan on using my  car for autocrossing and could use some help with any mods that I can do to help me out. I also have an 84 SE and an 87 that the vin says is a coupe. The 87 has a TEC4 engine and I was wondering if it can go into the 84 without to much trouble. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Toddster||07-15-2001||09:19 PM||||My '84 Indy has a "A" in the fourth position. The number series was a little screwed-up in '84. <P>It goes like this:<P>Position #1 = Nation of Origin<BR>#2 = Manufacturer (GM)<BR>#3 = Make and Type (Pontiac)<BR>#4 = Restraint System (A-non passive, B- passive/Auto belts, C-passive/inflatable restraints)<BR>#5 = Series Code (coupe = M, SE = F)<BR>#6&7 = Body Style (2-door notchback - 37)<BR>#8 = engine<BR>#9 = check digit<BR>#10 = year model<BR>#11 = Plant code (P - pontiac)<BR>#12-17 = sequential number||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex2004||07-15-2001||11:39 PM||||I also have an A in the 4th position, mine's an 84 SE.  VIN is 1g2af37r5ep263497  <P>Here is what Fiero.net gave me1 Made in USA  <BR>G Made by GM  <BR>2 Pontiac Division  <BR>A Fiero (P-Body)  <BR>F SE  <BR>37 NotchbackNotchback  <BR>R 2.5L L4 (LR8)  <BR>5 Check Digit  <BR>E 1984  <BR>P Made in Pontiac, MI  <BR>263497 63497 of 136,840  <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000009||Tweek||07-16-2001||11:08 AM||||I also have 1g2am... on my 84sc<P>1 Made in USA  <BR>G Made by GM  <BR>2 Pontiac Division  <BR>A Fiero (P-Body)  <BR>M Sport Coupe  <BR>37 NotchbackNotchback  <BR>R 2.5L L4 (LR8)  <BR>2 Check Digit  <BR>E 1984  <BR>P Made in Pontiac, MI  <BR>316131 116131 of 136,840  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Toddster||07-16-2001||12:11 PM||||Well, I'm reading from the actual 1984 Pontiac Service Manual and it says that the 4th position is for the restraint system.<P>Later year models changed. My '88 manual has the 4th position as the Series Code.<P>||||reg||1
